# Copy to `.env` and fill in. This is the file bootstrap.dart names when a key
# is missing, so it has to exist and it has to be current.
#
# EVERY KEY HERE SHIPS INSIDE THE APK. `.env` is declared under `flutter/assets`
# in pubspec.yaml, so the file is copied whole into the app bundle and into the
# web build — readable by anyone who unzips either. Three keys belong to that
# category and no fourth one does:
#
#   * the project URL and the anon/publishable key are PUBLIC by design. They
#     open nothing on their own; row-level security is what decides what a
#     request may see, and it runs on the server where the client cannot reach
#     it. Supabase publishes both in its own client-side quick-start.
#   * the Google web client ID is likewise public — it identifies the app to
#     Google, and the secret half of that pair never leaves Google's servers.
#
# Anything that grants rather than identifies — `service_role`, a database
# password, an FCM server key — goes in `.env.seed` instead (gitignored, never
# bundled), or into the server's own secret store via `supabase secrets set`.
#
# `test/env_secrets_test.dart` enforces this: it fails if `.env` carries a key
# no Dart file reads.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=
